steve rogers the world war ii hero and  perennial avenger known as captain  america  has been a cultural icon since he was  famously introduced  punching adolf hitler in the face on the  cover of captain america comics number  one  well you might already know about his  decades spent as an icicle or his  frenemy relationship with iron man  there's plenty of lesser-known details  about the sentinel of liberty  here is the untold truth of captain  america  before we get started does anyone want  to get out  he trains every avenger captain america  is among the finest hand-to-hand  combatants in the marvel universe  thanks to his vast experience training  and enhanced strength and reflexes  as such he trains just about every hero  who has come through the avengers  revolving door  among his more interesting students the  invincible iron man  she hulk hawkeye and even mary jane  watson  maybe he should be called drill sergeant  america your fighting style is to tackle  people or blast them  if i had to guess i'd say that you've  never been in an actual fight in your  life  multiple buckies almost as well known as  cap himself is his original sidekick  bucky barnes  barnes was a mascot at the military base  where rogers was stationed in the early  days of world war ii  who was taken under the captain's wings  bucky was presumed  dead along with cap in the fateful plane  crash that led to cap's hibernation  although the young sidekick would return  decades later as the winter soldier  lucky who the hell is bucky rogers would  eventually pick up another young  sidekick in the modern era  rick jones rick jones was directly  involved in the accident which  created the hulk and it was his distress  call which initially caused the avengers  to form  having been taken in by the team as an  honorary member  jones answered the call when cap found  himself in need of another partner  undergoing combat training and even for  a time wearing bucky's old uniform  the partnership didn't last long but  rick jones would continue to be a  sidekick for just about everyone in the  marvel universe  replaced by black panther in avengers  number 47  cap decides to take a leave of absence  from the team to set off on his own  adventures  a journey that would bring him to  wakanda where he would encounter perhaps  his only viable replacement  in black panther tell me captain america  is it really your shield after helping  cap to foil a plot by baron zemo to  destroy the united states using advanced  weaponry  t'challa accompanies cap back to america  mulling over his suggestion to join the  avengers as cap's replacement  t'challa quickly proves his worth in a  fight against the grim reaper and the  grateful team makes t'challa a  full-fledged member  after that cap would only make cameo  appearances in avengers comics until  returning to the team a full 3 years  later  the falcon and the red skull sam wilson  the falcon has been cap's staunchest  friend and ally  over the years their formal partnership  began way back in 1971's captain america  number 133  but strangely their long association  never would have happened if not for one  of the red skull's many evil plots to  kill captain america  in captain america number 117 steve  rogers is banished to a mysterious  island after getting his body switched  with the red skull  while there cap disguises himself as a  normal guy and runs into sam wilson a  harlem bird enthusiast who trains with  cap to become the falcon  together the two of them foil the red  skull's plot cap gets his body back and  sam wilson  embarks on a long crime fighting career  as the falcon  captain america and the captain americas  steve rogers might be the most famous  captain america but he's far from the  only one  after becoming disillusioned with  america and donning the new identity of  nomad  steve rogers left the captain america  identity available  and a trio of schmoes tried out for the  job while the first two bailed after  realizing just how perilous the job was  roscoe simmons received training from  the falcon himself  unfortunately he met a gruesome end at  the hands of the red skull  forcing rogers to return as captain  america to end the school's murderous  wrath  later wracked by fear of compromising  his principles he surrendered the  official captain america role to john  walker the super patriot  in favor of operating independently as  the captain  walker even kept cap's shield during  this time while rogers used a replica  john walker would later become u.s agent  once steve rogers returned to reclaim  the shield and trademark identity  in addition both bucky barnes and sam  wilson have likewise taken over the  mantle but rogers has always found his  way back from death  retirement or even just comic book limbo  you just don't know when to give up do  you do this all day  will the real cap please stand up in  2016  marvel used the relaunch title captain  america steve rogers to introduce the  most insanely controversial plot twist  in a history full of them  at the issue's end cap suddenly murders  his sidekick jack  flagg before uttering two words which  had cab fans the world over  reeling in shock hail hydra  it turned out that rogers had been  reconstructed by a sentient version of  the cosmic  cube after a near-death experience  unfortunately  the red skull had indoctrinated the cube  in one of the many times that he had  wielded it  causing roger's entire history to be  retconned as a hydra secret agent  as you might expect the real captain  america managed to escape his  imprisonment inside the cube's memory  and promptly defeated his fascist  counterpart  what makes the  chose to shield his shield must heal  cap's shield is perhaps the most iconic  tool in any superhero's arsenal  not only is it virtually indestructible  it can absorb vast amounts of kinetic  energy which is why it can withstand  blows from the hulk or thor without  simply sending cap flying  in its original comic incarnation the  shield isn't pure vibranium but an  alloy accidentally created by scientist  myron mclean  in a metallurgical accident mclean was  tasked by the us government with the  creation of a super strong metal to be  used in tanks  and one night while laboring over the  project mclean fell asleep  he awoke to find that the materials he'd  been working with had mysteriously  bonded  and cast the new substance using a disc  shaped mold for tank hatches  the government gifted cap with a shield  after he'd proven his metal in the field  and mclean was never able to duplicate  the process which created it  although repeated attempts would years  later result in the creation of  adamantium the famously strong metal of  which wolverine's skeleton is made  replicas of cap's shield would be  employed for various purposes over the  years but cap always preferred the real  deal  like the super soldier himself it's one  of a kind  shield throwing sense it's a common  misconception that cap's shield must be  equipped with some kind of technology to  make it return to him like a boomerang  but this isn't the case the shield's  ability to absorb and disperse kinetic  energy means that once bounced off an  object it will basically keep bouncing  forever until caught and cap's  understanding of its properties  enable him to predict its flight path  with unerring accuracy  handling it properly is practically a  superpower unto itself to the point  where even the two most accomplished  heroes to take up cap's mantle  sam wilson and bucky barnes both  struggled mightily to learn how to use  it as an offensive weapon  even with extensive training from rogers  however there is one avenger for whom  handling the shield wasn't much of a  problem  clint barton hawkeye perhaps the one  hero whose mastery of physics and  ballistics is on par with caps  leave it to the most underrated avenger  to measure up to cap's exacting  standards  [Music]  thanks for watching click the looper  icon to subscribe to our youtube channel  plus check out all this cool stuff we  know you'll love too  [Music]
 

